# Paths where a human must look before merge.
#
# Not bureaucracy. Three vulnerability classes shipped to main in code that was
# merged, CI-green, and covered by tests that looked adequate — impersonation,
# room access, and no-eject — and none were caught by review. Everywhere else can
# auto-merge on green CI; these paths keep the one check that has ever worked.

# All cryptography.
/crates/cairn-crypto/                @superwilso

# Authentication, membership, and the rules the server enforces.
/crates/cairn-server/src/state.rs    @superwilso
/crates/cairn-server/src/storage.rs  @superwilso

# Canonical signing bytes and the tier model. A change here can silently
# invalidate every signature or weaken a tier.
/crates/cairn-proto/src/envelope.rs  @superwilso
/crates/cairn-proto/src/tier.rs      @superwilso

# The document every security claim is measured against.
/docs/01-threat-model.md             @superwilso
/SECURITY.md                         @superwilso
